            "text": "{\"description\":\"The visible face of the stone has shallow relief carvings divided into horizontal bands. Along the upper band are several arch-topped shapes, and below them are multiple animal-like figures with long necks or beak-like heads, plus small rounded depressions or circles. The lower visible area continues with worn animal-like and linear carvings, partly obscured by adjacent stones and damage.\",\"avian\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"Several figures have birdlike long necks and beak-like heads; one is clearly visible on the lower left of the main carved face.\",\"box\":[0.28,0.74,0.45,0.93]},\"large_face\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"No large human face with eyes, nose, and mouth is visible on the main surface; the carvings appear to be animals, arches, and abstract/linear forms.\",\"box\":null},\"scorpion\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"Some worn linear animal forms could be read in different ways, but I cannot clearly identify a scorpion with legs and a segmented upturned tail.\",\"box\":null},\"round_motif\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"A distinct small circular motif is visible near the middle of the carved surface, separate from any clear eye or nostril.\",\"box\":[0.38,0.38,0.45,0.44]},\"three_arches\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"The top band contains three or more repeated arch-topped forms side by side.\",\"box\":[0.19,0.08,0.73,0.29]},\"limitations\":\"The relief is worn and low-contrast, lighting is uneven, and parts of the stone are obscured by foreground rocks and edge damage, making some figures ambiguous.\"}",
